WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.540
For Christmas, from her mom,

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.940
Katherine received a log book that once contained records from her grandmother's hair salon.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.820
After she had kids, though, she turned it into a recipe book,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.980
pasting in recipes from newspapers and magazines from the  '40s and '50s

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.780
They are...interesting, so Katherine and I decided to try a few of 'em out

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.800
The results were mixed. Here is our journey.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:28.980
[music]

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.340
Recipe 1 - Golden Rabbit. You make it with two Campbell's soups

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.280
Stir WELL.
One can Campbell's Cheddar Cheese soup.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.720
GRADUALLY blend in 1 can Campbell's Tomato soup.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.400
Add 1 quarter cup of milk

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:42.900
Heat

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.540
Stirring

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.380
Pour over crackers or toast

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.160
Mmhmm, Good.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.080
Hank: Bland
Katherine: Yeah, it's not a lot of flavor.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.420
Hank: I have injured myself.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.160
I got too excited about my Golden Rabbit

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.900
Doesn't it look like a golden rabbit?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.620
Katherine: This is not on the list of things that I
want to eat again.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.040
Hank: The predominant flavor is crackers

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.280
Katherine: Well, I do like crackers.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.120
It grows on you.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.680
Hank: You still hungry? Just add more crackers.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.160
Katherine: Serve it with half a raw potato.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.920
Hank: Recipe number 2 - Popovers

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.260
In a bowl, dump one cup unsifted flour, one half teaspoon salt,

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:09.760
2 eggs

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.640
(Just break them over the bowl and drop them in so they're staring at you with their big yellow eyes)

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.360
1 cup milk.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.380
Beat this with an eggbeater till it's just mixed.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.760
Now fill the cups half-full,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.800
and set the cookie sheet in the 450˚ oven.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.660
You will have 6 splendid popovers

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:22.820
so golden-brown

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.740
and exuberantly puffed up that it's almost embarrassing.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.960
I kind of burned them.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:27.460
Katherine: Yeah

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.980
Hank: You know, tastes like bread.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.080
Katherine: Huh, Northern biscuit.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:30.880
Hank: I'm down with this

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:31.380
Katherine: Yeah

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.760
I'd like to try them again.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.720
Hank: Hole in the middle?

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.740
Katherine: Hole in the middle

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.700
Hank: I don't why it's got a hole in the middle

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.580
Ha-owwww!

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.680
Hahaha

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.420
Recipe number 3 - Beer Dressing

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.780
Mix mayonnaise and mustard together, add horseradish and gradually stir in beer.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.000
I mean...it's not good

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.440
I don't really like mustard that much though.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.800
Recipe number 4 - Mexican Chop Suey

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.020
1/2 pound ground beef fried in butter when possible.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.960
1 cup sliced fresh tomatoes, 1 medium sweet PAPPER

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.920
1/2 cup chopped onion, 1/2 cup chopped celery, 1 cup milk, 1 tablespoon flour

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.180
Fry the meat slowly over low heat, then remove the meat, leaving the juices,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.160
to which should be added the vegetable ingredients,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.600
Simmer until tender, add tomatoes, after which add milk,

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.100
mixed with flour, and simmer again until mixture begins to thicken like gravy.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.020
Then combine with meat and serve immediately

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.840
You seem really unexcited about this one.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.180
It said to serve immediately, so we can't dilly-dally

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.740
This is probably the best it's ever gonna be

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.440
Katherine: It smells like...dog food.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.440
You just went right for it, huh?

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.660
(laughs)

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.460
Hank: I have a suggestion for improving it.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.300
Huge amounts

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.720
Katherine: (laughs)

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:30.240
Hank: -of salt

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.540
Katherine: You gonna - yeah - eat more?

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:32.620
Hank: It-it's so much better

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.640
Katherine: Right now you're wasting salt

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.860
Hank: I maybe over-salted mine

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.900
Katherine: Yeah, you really went to town on it.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.540
Hank: Katherine, if you were gonna name this dish,

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.340
what would you call it?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.900
Obviously it is inspired both by Chinese food and Mexican food.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.400
Katherine: N-W-what?

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:47.160
N-no, it loo- It's like uhh Cleveland...Chowder

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.220
Hank: (laughs)

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.340
Recipe number 5 - Orange Cranberry Relish Mold

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.740
Dissolve gelatin in boiling water, add orange juice and chill until consistency of unbeaten egg white,

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.400
Cut orange in quarters, remove seeds and put through a food chopper.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.000
Add ground orange, cranberry sauce, celery and nuts to gelatin mixture

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.920
and turn into a 1-quart mold.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.620
Chill until firm. Unmold to serve.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.520
Katherine: Oooh, nooo (laughs)

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.940
Hank: It's...like...a colon!

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.280
(laughs) it feels like

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:18.580
Ohhh

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.060
It's like coming across, just some sand in your food.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.340
Do not serve your friends or family this.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.840
Katherine: Why does Jell-O even still exist?

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.120
Awww - This is what you get if you're - I it's okay! -  in prison,

